<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed weaker at 1.40 pct below parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed weaker at 1.40 pct below parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland (NBP) fixed the zloty at 3.4705 to the dollar, down from 3.4380 previously, and at 1.8800 to the mark, down from 1.8720, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 1.40 percent below the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, weaker than Friday's fix at -0.81 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
